---
layout: base.njk
pagination:
  data: sections
  size: 1
  addAllPagesToCollections: true
  alias: s
permalink: "{{ s.url }}"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ s.title }}"
  description: "{{ s.description }}"
  breadcrumbs:
    - { label: "Writing", url: "/writing/" }
sections:
  - url: /scholarship/
    title: Scholarship
    lede: Peer-reviewed sociology, and two research platforms — Doing Modernity, on Critical Interactionism and the Santa Barbara School, and Wild Flesh, on critical drug studies.
    description: "Scholarship by Wayne Martin Mellinger, Ph.D.: peer-reviewed publications, Doing Modernity and Wild Flesh, and his work in Critical Interactionism, ethnomethodology and conversation analysis, homelessness and institutional abandonment, and critical drug studies."
    collections: [scholarship, doing-modernity, wild-flesh]
    programs: [critical-interactionism, interaction-emca, homelessness-abandonment, critical-drug-studies]
  - url: /public-writing/
    title: Public Writing
    lede: Writing for a general audience — mostly Noozhawk columns on homelessness, housing, mental health and civic life in Santa Barbara.
    description: "Public writing by Wayne Martin Mellinger, Ph.D.: Noozhawk columns on homelessness, housing, mental health and civic life in Santa Barbara."
    collections: [noozhawk]
    programs: [public-sociology-justice]
    note: Wayne’s fourth platform, Our Neighbors on the Streets, has not yet been catalogued here.
  - url: /religion-philosophy/
    title: Religion & Philosophy
    lede: Religious naturalism, contemporary Paganism and ecstatic spiritual practice — the theological framework Wayne calls Dionysian Naturalism.
    description: "Writing by Wayne Martin Mellinger, Ph.D., on religious naturalism, Dionysian Naturalism and spiritual practice, from The Dionysian Naturalist."
    collections: [dionysian-naturalist]
    programs: [religious-dionysian-naturalism]
  - url: /creative-work/
    title: Creative Work
    lede: Poetry, prayer and ritual writing.
    description: "Poetry, prayers and ritual writing by Wayne Martin Mellinger, from Moments of Awe Punctuated by the Mundane (2025) and The Dionysian Naturalist."
    collections: [poetry]
    creative: true
---
<header class="page-head">
  <p class="eyebrow">Writing</p>
  <h1>{{ s.title }}</h1>
  <p class="lede">{{ s.lede }}</p>
</header>

<section aria-labelledby="where">
  <h2 id="where" class="label">{{ "Collections" if s.collections.length > 1 else "Collection" }}</h2>
  <ul class="cards">
    {%- for slug in s.collections %}{% set c = archive.collectionBySlug[slug] %}
    <li class="card">
      <h3><a href="{{ c.path }}">{{ c.title }}</a></h3>
      <p>{{ c.intro }}</p>
      <p class="count">{{ archive.byCollection[slug].length | pluralize(c.noun) }}</p>
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
  {%- if s.note %}<p class="coverage">{{ s.note }}</p>{% endif %}
</section>

{%- if s.programs %}
<section aria-labelledby="bodies">
  <h2 id="bodies" class="label">Bodies of work</h2>
  <ul class="program-list">
    {%- for slug in s.programs %}{% set pp = archive.programPageBySlug[slug] %}
    <li><a href="{{ pp.path }}">{{ pp.name }}</a> <span class="count">{{ pp.works.length }}</span>
      <p>{{ pp.description }}</p></li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>
{%- endif %}

{%- if s.creative %}
<section aria-labelledby="books">
  <h2 id="books" class="label">Books</h2>
  <ul class="program-list">
    <li><cite>Moments of Awe Punctuated by the Mundane</cite> (2025). Poems. <a href="/creative-work/poetry/">Read a selection</a>; the full collection is available from Wayne on request.</li>
    <li><a href="https://philarchive.org/rec/MELIJW"><cite>I Just Wanted to Dance with Dionysus: Life’s Sacred Journey, Lost Souls and Our Thirst for Wholeness</cite></a> (2025). A Gonzo autoethnography.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="prayers" id="prayers-section">
  <h2 id="prayers" class="label">Prayers &amp; ritual</h2>
  <p>Prayer runs through both platforms — ritual writing from <cite>The Dionysian Naturalist</cite> alongside prayer-poems from <cite>Moments of Awe</cite>.</p>
  <ul class="program-list">
    {%- set clue = archive.byId['dn-santa-barbara-rising-opening-prayer-for-clue'] %}
    {%- set muse = archive.byId['poem-invocation-to-the-earth-muse'] %}
    {%- if clue %}<li><a href="{{ clue.url }}">{{ clue.title }}</a> <span class="work-venue">The Dionysian Naturalist, {{ clue | dateLabel(true) }}</span></li>{% endif %}
    {%- if muse %}<li><a href="{{ muse.page }}">{{ muse.title }}</a> <span class="work-venue">Poem, {{ muse | dateLabel(true) }}</span></li>{% endif %}
  </ul>
  <p class="coverage">Also in <cite>Moments of Awe</cite>, not yet on this site: “A Prayer for Those Who Serve,” “Prayer for Longest Night,” and “A Prayer for an Entheogenic Sacrament.”</p>
</section>
{%- endif %}
